Subject: [PATCH 07994/11362] [outer-loop] gateway-accurate re-score: the
 OPENING reset is FREE, so my own 4.6% correction was overstated (3.69%)

A NUMBER I REPORTED THIS SESSION MOVES, AND IT IS NAMED FIRST IN THE ARTIFACT. Commit e871f32be
shipped "the uncharged-RESET optimism is 4.6% (measured)". That charged EVERY reset. The installed
gateway gives the opening one away free: update_scorecard (arc_agi/scorecard.py:834-843) routes a
RESET to new_play() when full_reset is true and to reset() otherwise; only reset() reaches
inc_reset_count, and new_play -> inc_play_count (:692-699) APPENDS a zeroed counter row and
increments nothing. full_reset is true exactly when the env is CREATED (api.py:405-437), and the
reference agent opens with an empty guid and a RESET. One free reset per play.

CORRECTED, same 44 matched live cells: median 4.62% -> 3.69%, max 16.80% -> 16.61%, non-zero
42/44 -> 38/44. Per-game median-of-medians 4.92% -> 3.68%. The defect is real; the published figure
was too PESSIMISTIC.

THE PUBLISHED MODEL IS UNREACHABLE, NOT CONSERVATIVE -- a computed witness, not an argument. Driving
the real Scorecard with a first update_scorecard(RESET, full_reset=False) raises KeyError: no card
exists, because that RESET is the call that CREATES the play. Reproducing it needs a phantom
new_play() the gateway never performs, and the artifact says so in the field where it does it.

A SECOND, INDEPENDENT ERROR in the per-span artifact's figure: it differenced two 4-DECIMAL-ROUNDED
scores. tu93's published 0.041667 is literally 0.0003/0.0072; unrounded it is 0.046236. Rounding and
charge model are now reported separately per cell so neither is credited with the other's movement.

THE HIGHER-SEVERITY CORRECTION IS IN CODE AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT LANDED HERE.
scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py charges the opening reset, so EVERY row it writes from now on has an
efficiency_gateway_charged that is too low. The minimal fix is specified field-by-field in
CORRECTION_OWED.claim_3. Not applied in this commit because that file is a freshness-tracked
dependency of five committed artifacts plus one uncommitted peer artifact; editing it would mark them
all stale in the same commit that publishes the correction. Top follow-up.

THREE INDEPENDENT REPRODUCTIONS of the prior lane's numbers, which is what licenses reading the
difference as a charge-model change rather than a pipeline difference: Part A's bound distribution
bit-identical at all seven quantiles (n=485, median 0.113725, max 0.956551, mean 0.204208); Part B's
unrounded M1 median exactly 0.046236; the cumulative and per-span attribution channels agreeing 7/7.

THE BOUND IS STAMPED UNINFORMATIVE, NOT QUOTED. Best case 0 BY CONSTRUCTION, worst case 95%+, so it
establishes neither materiality nor negligibility -- which is exactly what justified instrumenting.

I SHIPPED A DEFECT AND THE REAL CHAIN CAUGHT IT. The path-2 frame builder hardcoded
levels_completed=0 on non-final span frames. set_levels_completed appends on any CHANGE in either
direction and the scorer consumes actions_by_level POSITIONALLY, so a spurious (0,16) entry turned a
2.09 score into 21.31. A calculator-only path would have hidden it. Regression-tested both ways.

A MUTATION ESCAPED MY OWN SUITE and is recorded rather than quietly fixed: hardcoding
chain_agrees_M1: True survived a test asserting the flag was True AND that both path scores matched,
because they genuinely did. Caught only by a third test that makes path 2 return a wrong score. 10/10
mutations now proved caught.

Nothing submitted. MAX_ACTIONS and every SUBMITTED_* flag untouched. No historical artifact's numbers
rewritten -- originals cited by path + sha256, M1 published beside M2 rather than over it. Closes
REQ-ARC-WMTE-5985 limitation (7); adds REQ-ARC-WMTE-5986 + 5 SCENARIOs, 19 tests.

